WHY THIS ATTEMPT EXISTS
  Attempt 1 produced a report.docx in which the ten evidence captures did not
  render in Microsoft Word. The document text, tables, hashes and layout were
  correct; only the images were invisible.

  Cause. The capture files are named "homepage" with no file extension. The
  docx writer derives each media part name from the source filename, so the
  captures were stored as word/media/image2. through word/media/image10., with
  an empty extension. [Content_Types].xml carries a Default for "png" but
  nothing that resolves an empty extension, and no Override was written for
  those parts, so their content type is undefined. Word will not render a part
  whose content type it cannot resolve. LibreOffice sniffs the leading bytes
  instead and rendered them, which is why the attempt-1 PDF check passed and
  the defect reached the operator.

  Attempt 1 verified that the capture bytes were present inside the package and
  that a LibreOffice render showed them. Neither check can fail on this defect.
  The missing check was whether every media part has a resolvable content type.

FIX
  Each capture is copied to a byte-identical <sha256>.png file and embedded from
  that path, so the media parts are now word/media/imageN.png and resolve
  against the existing png Default. Nothing else changed: no content, no
  wording, no subcategory, no keyword, no timestamp, no layout.

  The capture bytes are unchanged, so every SHA-256 evidence hash printed in the
  report still describes the embedded capture, and spec rule 10 (embed the
  capture exactly as taken) continues to hold. Verified by hashing every
  word/media part against the source evidence files: all 10 match, records 7 and
  10 correctly share one part because their captures are byte-identical.

CHECKS ADDED THIS ATTEMPT
  - every word/media part resolves to a content type via a Default or Override
    in [Content_Types].xml                                        10/10 OK
  - every r:embed id in document.xml resolves in document.xml.rels 11/11 OK
  - 11 w:drawing elements present (crest + 10 captures)            OK

